{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/568618-how-weird-are-your-solar-anima-banners","id":568618,"title":"How \"weird\" are your Solar Anima Banners?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-25T18:57:47-07:00","id":568618,"title":"How \"weird\" are your Solar Anima Banners?","content":"Man, I sure am asking a lot of questions lately. Here's another one: What are the criteria for Solar anima banners? Can they really be anything (appropriate) that comes to mind? Or are there limits? Most I see are pretty down to earth, but what about those that are really &quot;out there&quot;? What's the strangest Solar anima banner you've made?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/899-the-free-man","name":"The Free Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar899_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T20:09:34-07:00","id":568688,"title":"","content":"The guideline in the 2E core is just that it's &quot;iconic&quot; to the character. The given examples include both something representative (a bull) and something abstract (a mandala). There's a lot of room for interpretation in that.<br /> <br /> I favor abstract and weird, but that's just me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T20:11:56-07:00","id":568692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Free Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/568618-how-weird-are-your-solar-anima-banners#post568618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the criteria for Solar anima banners?</div> </div> </div> </div>Your imagination is the limit. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Free Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/568618-how-weird-are-your-solar-anima-banners#post568618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can they really be anything (appropriate) that comes to mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're <i>probably not</i> going to be a depiction of a demon, but you never know. A skillful brawler may have an anima that looks like a blood ape <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Free Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/568618-how-weird-are-your-solar-anima-banners#post568618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or are there limits?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean...there shouldn't be. This is a reflection of the character's soul and nature. Limits just shut down interesting stories. Further, the banner imagine is pure fluff. A restriction on that doesn't accomplish anything except constraint.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Free Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/568618-how-weird-are-your-solar-anima-banners#post568618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the strangest Solar anima banner you've made?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a tribal, Wyld-y phenotype (from a people basically bred by a Lunar) desert shaman Zenith whose anima banner is a giant cactus in full bloom.<br /> <br /> I have a Dawn whose anima banner is basically a Germanic double-headed screaming eagle. Not sure if I want it to have 2 wings or 4-6. <br /> <br /> There are probably more, just can't think of them at this time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T20:32:31-07:00","id":568697,"title":"","content":"I'm waiting for someone to try and use their anima banner as a facebook wall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T21:21:37-07:00","id":568749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/568618-how-weird-are-your-solar-anima-banners?p=568697#post568697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm waiting for someone to try and use their anima banner as a facebook wall.</div> </div> </div> </div>An renowned Eclipse, blood-brothers with eagles and merfolk alike, who has traversed all directions of Creation and made many allies. His anima is a tapestry, a melting pot of fur, leaves, light, and textiles, shifting about him in a protective cloak- never the same patterns twice. <i>Do not harm our friend, </i>it says silently. <i>He is beloved.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T21:32:57-07:00","id":568755,"title":"","content":"The oddest I have had was not an image. It changed the environment to make material appear to be of higher quality. Cheap earthenware looks like porcelain, dull granite walls appear to be alabaster, dull bronze looks like gold, etc. The idea was that for that brief moment when it flared totemic people would literally see the glory the Solars bring to the world. (Zenith)<br /> <br /> Another was a clockwork sun with a large corona of old realm equations. (Twilight)<br /> <br /> An emerald aurora through which could be seen a silver stars and flashes of things lost or longed for. (Malefactor)<br /> <br /> Green and white fire that flowed over the ground and up surrounding objects so that the area appeared to be within a primordial temple. That was actually the standard buildup rather than the icon. The iconic itself ramped it up to a full fledged structure. (Defiler)<br /> <br /> Electric blue magnetic field lines that hit surfaces and flowed like ripples (Orichalcum)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T21:43:34-07:00","id":568760,"title":"","content":"One of my PCs (a Lunar) has a banner that resembles an falcon with two snakes entwined about its wings. As a fight gets more intense, the snakes and bird blend together until it becomes a scaled, winged, two-headed falcon with snake fangs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Murcushio: Sure, you avoid all that messy withdrawal, but you still need to <i>stop doing heroin</i> (for the purposes of this discussion your cousin is named Heroin).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4657-maxastro","name":"MaxAstro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4657_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T23:12:49-07:00","id":568829,"title":"","content":"i had in mind for my sideral (The most useless and complete idiot of the creation) to have a Sock Puppet with googly eyes as his anima banner. That or a piece of wood with a face draw into it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T02:08:14-07:00","id":568936,"title":"","content":"the ones i remember from my team:<br /> <br /> 16 different pairs of swords, like the ones on the FF XIII promotional video. (twilight)<br /> <br /> A cape that is a reflection of a starred night sky (night)<br /> <br /> Diablos from FF VIII (twilight)<br /> <br /> Baphomet from ragnarok online (dawn)<br /> <br /> Carmen Electra (Dawn, and the fear effect was her stripping her panties and revealing a huge d...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/278-elyon","name":"Elyon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar278_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T03:02:46-07:00","id":568957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/568618-how-weird-are-your-solar-anima-banners?p=568829#post568829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i had in mind for my sideral (The most useless and complete idiot of the creation) to have a Sock Puppet with googly eyes as his anima banner. That or a piece of wood with a face draw into it</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereals don't have an iconic display for their anima - the area of illumination just increases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T04:00:09-07:00","id":568996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/568618-how-weird-are-your-solar-anima-banners?p=568957#post568957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereals don't have an iconic display for their anima - the area of illumination just increases.</div> </div> </div> </div>boooooooooring","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T04:23:21-07:00","id":569019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Free Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/568618-how-weird-are-your-solar-anima-banners#post568618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How &quot;weird&quot; are your Solar Anima Banners?</div> </div> </div> </div>My iconic display is of Sir Douglas Bader jumping a motorcycle through a flaming ring while flipping everyone the bird. Of course, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kEGuHdKn0Lc\" target=\"_blank\">music plays</a> when this happens.<br /> <br /> Oh, you mean my <i>PCs\u2019</i> animas!<br /> <br /> I usually just go for animals or abstract symbols.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T05:38:33-07:00","id":569091,"title":"","content":"I think probably the &quot;weirdest&quot; one I've had in game was a character that was a disgraced executioner (I may, or may not, have been watching/reading a lot of Lone Wolf and Cub at the time) who's Icon was brilliant glowing High Realm calligraphy stating the names of everyone he had extinguished the life of all over his person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T05:48:53-07:00","id":569103,"title":"","content":"Oh, thought of another one. The character was an occult investigator. Her anima was a roiling blanket of different human and animal eyes of varying sizes, constantly glancing around in all directions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T07:48:37-07:00","id":569199,"title":"","content":"Let's see. The two weirdest I've seen were a chicken (no, not a proud rooster or mother hen, just a chicken) and a Twilight who declared her anima was a giant book with fangs.<br /> <br /> The weirdest one I think I've done was a no moon lunar with the spirit shape of lamb, whose anima was his spirit shape who would rear up, rampant, and then serenely spill its viscera and blood on the ground in mystically significant patterns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T08:01:35-07:00","id":569207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">boooooooooring</div> </div> </div> </div> I appreciate at least one approach to Animas that is more subdued and lacks ostentatious details. It's always a certain tension I feel with regards to depiction of magic, so to diversify the things a bit appeals to me, and it feels suitable for Sidereals to be the ones with it. I also think there's room for variations in tone and intensity in the colouring, and the idea of a more subtle kind of symbolism being evident also appeals to me. It's like comparing classical painting to abstract expressionism; I wouldn't call &quot;Who's Afraid of Red, Yellow and Blue&quot; boring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T10:05:56-07:00","id":569362,"title":"","content":"A by-no-means complete list of some I've seen or heard about, from the most basic :<br /> - A glorious golden warrior wielding flaming twin swords, reproducing each move the character made<br /> - A eternally rebirthing phoenix, burning then ashes then firebird and burning again<br /> - A rainbow serpent with ten thousand eyes<br /> - A mandala of golden runes in an unknow language<br /> <br /> to the elaborate :<br /> - A clockwork serpent crowned by blue-green flames<br /> - A great tree populated with animals from all around the world, one of them (never the same) meditating on the highest branch<br /> - A storm of written oaths whirling together in the shape of a great hawk<br /> <br /> to the dowright weird :<br /> - The life-size plans of a celestial, creation-wide machine (strange in that the machine doesn't move with the anima : instead, the light of the anima shows the machine around the Exalt : should he move, another part of the machine is lit and visible)<br /> - A great door that absorbs and destroy all roads that do not lead towards it, opening on unknown vistas<br /> - A shining fog where one can glimpse vision of their worst fears.<br /> <br /> So yeah... as long as they reflect something cool about the charater, animas can pretty much encompass anything you can imagine for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":541,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","user":"LeTipex","date":". 06-26-2015, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T11:10:51-07:00","id":571697,"title":"","content":"My weirdest two no longer seem wierd... But anyway, my Zenith's anima banner was a set of white and gold vestments that shaped themselves to whatever he was wearing at the time. They were solid at dramatic moments, but faded to shining outlines otherwise. They also included armor when he used Glorious Solar Plate.<br /> <br /> My Dawn had a pair of golden tigers (as in full-on tigers made of golden light with red stripes) that reacted to whatever he did. they circled him normally, pounced when he attacked, roared battle cries with him. They were also semi-tangible to him, as he would occasionally pet them absentmindedly when his anima was up but his blood was calm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Life before Death, Strength before Weakness, Journey before Destination.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">&quot;I will protect those who cannot protect themselves&quot;</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4172-marros56","name":"Marros56","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4172_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T11:25:18-07:00","id":571707,"title":"","content":"My Eclipse's anima was an empty crystalline silhouette of a 20-foot burning devil holding books and scrolls of law. Like a human <a href=\"https://fnmalafarina.files.wordpress.com/2012/03/nicol-bolas-portrait.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Nicol Bolas</a> lawyer.<br /> <br /> My Night's anima was an oil-black snarling Manticore that would burst into (and materialize from) bats. Both &quot;forms&quot; had wings with twinkling golden stars on the inside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T14:02:45-07:00","id":571855,"title":"","content":"Still a little bit proud of the one that was seven broken crane wings, which she occasionally interacted with in using Glorious Solar Saber.<br /> <br /> I mean, normally you'd think that a Solar having the soul of the Broken-Winged Crane would be something to run away from really fast, but this particular game was a one with (slightly) friendlier Yozis who had taken in the remaining human populations after Creation was destroyed, so even though it wasn't spelled out in exact terms &quot;the story of our glorious return&quot; made for something of a messianic figure.<br /> <br /> (She became an akuma in pretty much every other iteration of the universe, though. Funny how that works!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T14:06:34-07:00","id":571860,"title":"","content":"I had a Solar whose Anima didn't produce a visual effect - it produced background music. Dramatic trumpets would start blaring whenever he flared.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T15:20:24-07:00","id":571930,"title":"","content":"I was always slightly disappointed that anima banners for Solars are visual displays and nothing else. Like, as cheesy as this sounds, I think it's kind of a letdown my anima banner can't be fucking theme music, you know? Like, when I go iconic, why can't <a href=\"https://youtu.be/TRT4rZMlTGc?t=36\" target=\"_blank\">this music</a> start playing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":271,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","user":"JimB","date":". 06-28-2015, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T15:23:06-07:00","id":571933,"title":"","content":"I think the anima of the Sun God's Chosen should absolutely have a major glowing golden light effect. But theme music should totally be allowed for the iconic banner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T16:01:46-07:00","id":571983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/568618-how-weird-are-your-solar-anima-banners?p=571933#post571933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the anima of the Sun God's Chosen should absolutely have a major glowing golden light effect. But theme music should totally be allowed for the iconic banner.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, dramatic wind that makes their clothes billow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}